{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968574-scottish-and-irish-accents","id":968574,"title":"Scottish and Irish Accents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-13T09:41:18-07:00","id":968574,"title":"Scottish and Irish Accents","content":"My NWO Operative is from the Isle of Man, and if I understood the concept of the Connachta correctly, also has Scottish relatives somewhere in his family tree. How do you write Scotch and Irish accents without being completely impenetrable? (Although I did understand the subtitles in Trainspotting.) How many dialects and languages is Maury likely to know? Also, if anyone can point me towards any good books on Irish and Scottish history, I would appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","user":"Saint Michael","date":". 09-13-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:05:13-07:00","id":968588,"title":"","content":"Ye canna put th' wyrds doon ta pap'r eas'ly, boyo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:39:50-07:00","id":968610,"title":"","content":"I would recommend not writing accents phonetically. Even when it isn't difficult to read, it's still annoying at best and offensive at worst. You can convey accents just as effectively with word choice (for example, &quot;yourself&quot; instead of &quot;you&quot; and &quot;I'm after&quot; instead of &quot;I just&quot; are two easily recognizable irishisms) and narration (&quot;Joseph said in a lilt much thicker than his cousin's.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:41:44-07:00","id":968646,"title":"","content":"I usually use do use narration; I just thought accents might work too. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:42:16-07:00","id":968647,"title":"","content":"The key Scottish phrase is 'outwith' instead of... 'outside' or maybe 'aside'. It's a word that's totally foreign to me as someone who grew up in England but you'll find it everywhere in Scotland, even in the official documents.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, an NWO agent is likely to be pretty well educated and those inpenetrable accents tend to be a working-class phenomena. 'Outwith' is the one outlier I've found in that educated Scots and state organisations will use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and if I understood the concept of the Connachta correctly, </div> </div> </div>Is that a WoD term?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/968574-scottish-and-irish-accents#post968574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if anyone can point me towards any good books on Irish and Scottish history, I would appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What broadly are you looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T12:00:27-07:00","id":968661,"title":"","content":"The Connachta were a group of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connachta\" target=\"_blank\">Irish dynasties</a>, at least according to